    "title": "Tornado Causes Damage in Largo, Florida",
    "text": "Trending Story\nUpdated 04:16 AM UTC, Thu June 26, 2025\nTornado Causes Damage in Largo, Florida\nLARGO, Fla. – Largo Fire Rescue crews are currently on the scene assessing significant storm-related damage at Ranchero Village and Bay Ranch Manufactured Home Communities, located on the 7000 Block of Ulmerton Road. The emergency response was initiated at approximately 7:20 PM tonight following reports of the widespread damage.\nSteve Ewing\n\"I’m watching TV and all of a sudden, it’s like a freight train, that’s the best way to describe it.\"\nRobert Sullivan\n\"We came out here and looked up in the sky, and there was like a huge cyclone of just parts and stuff flying in the air that was probably 2,000 feet high.\"\nComments\nTim\nYep\n1\nTim\nCrazy for sure.\n1\nTim\nAnd we had hail too.\n1",
